{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, `y ~ normal(mu, sigma)`, after both parameters have their built-in priors. The remaining data variables (`N`, `mu0`, `lambda0`, `alpha0`, `beta0`) are context inputs used as sizes or hyperparameters and are not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  vector[N] y;
  real mu0;
  real<lower=0> lambda0;
  real<lower=0> alpha0;
  real<lower=0> beta0;
}
parameters {
  real mu;
  real<lower=0> tau;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma = inv_sqrt(tau);
}
model {
  tau ~ gamma(alpha0, beta0);
  mu ~ normal(mu0, inv_sqrt(lambda0 * tau));
  y ~ normal(mu, sigma);
}
generated quantities {
  real y_rep = normal_rng(mu, sigma);
}
